# The null and bool singletons must never lose reference counts through a
# slot. A heap-tagged singleton slot lost one count per pop: 1.1M builtin
# calls on a null argument drove the null singleton's 1000000 to zero and
# free()d a static (EigenLua warmup pairs fuzz, 2026-10-11). Each loop runs
# past the 1000000 margin, so a regression aborts here.

n is null
b is 1 == 1
i is 0
loop while i < 1050000:
    t is type of n
    u is type of b
    i is i + 1

xs is [0]
d is {"k": 0}
j is 0
loop while j < 1050000:
    xs[0] is n
    d["k"] is b
    j is j + 1

if t == "null" and u == "bool" and xs[0] == null and d["k"]:
    print of "All tests passed"
